IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sda-common`
IMPORT `taa-procedure`
IMPORT `sda-home`
IMPORT `sda-vehicles`

-- Stamp Duty Act 1978 (NT) with the Taxation Administration Act 2007 (NT) -- the individual's questions.
--
-- SEAT: the individual buyer and taxpayer -- the conveyee of a home in the Territory (the person to whom the land is
-- conveyed, liable for the duty under s 50(a)), or the applicant registering a motor vehicle (liable under s 57(1)); and
-- as taxpayer, or as applicant for a first home owner grant, the person affected by a decision under TAA Part 11. "What
-- do I pay? What relief do I get? When must I lodge, pay and notify? How do I challenge it?" Every question is phrased
-- as that person would ask it, on facts that person could state. The rules are in sda-home.l4, sda-vehicles.l4 and
-- taa-procedure.l4; this module builds their records from plain answers and restates no rule.
--
-- THE NORTHERN TERRITORY LEVIES NO LAND TAX, so there is no land tax question here (unlike Western Australia). For a
-- purchase signed after 30 June 2021 no Part 5 Division 2 home concession is open (s 88A); the live relief for a
-- buyer now is the s 90D exemption for a new home bought from a building contractor (1 July 2022 to 30 June 2027).
--
-- GENERATED by scratchpad au-nt-1/gen_seat.py so that each question carries the same seat-worded inputs.
--
