-- Northern Territory (see SOURCE-LICENSE.md). BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Stamp Duty Act 1978 and Taxation Administration Act 2007 (NT) -- the buyer's and taxpayer's questions`

-- Answers that only the seat needs.
DECLARE `Entitlement answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes, apart from s 90B: only the one concession of greatest benefit can be had`
    `no`
    `not covered here` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

DECLARE `Notice answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: written notice to the Commissioner within this many days after it first becomes apparent, or a fine of up to this many penalty units` HAS `days` IS A NUMBER, `penalty units` IS A NUMBER
    `no notice is required of me`

GIVEN `the date the contract or transfer was first signed` IS A DATE @desc The day the first document for your purchase (usually the contract) was signed by everyone, as a date (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-15)
      `the price` IS A NUMBER @desc The price you are paying for the property, in Australian dollars, including any GST; 0 if it is a gift
      `the value of the property` IS A NUMBER @desc The full market value of the property free of any mortgage or other encumbrance, in Australian dollars, including GST (if you do not know it, give the price)
      `there is already a home on the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a home on the land when the contract is signed (answer no for vacant land or a home still to be built)
      `I am buying off the plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your contract is to buy a home not yet occupied or sold, on a proposed lot of a plan of subdivision, survey or units plan (an off-the-plan contract)
      `every buyer is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and every co-buyer are individuals (not a company or a trust)
      `at least one buyer is 18 or older` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or at least one co-buyer is 18 or older on the day the contract is signed (or the Commissioner has exempted you from the age requirement)
      `at least one buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or at least one co-buyer is an Australian citizen or a permanent resident
      `at least one buyer is 60 or older` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or at least one co-buyer is 60 or older on the day the contract is signed
      `at least one buyer holds an NT concession card` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or a co-buyer holds an NT Pensioner and Carer Concession Card or a Northern Territory Concession Scheme Card (an administrative scheme of the Territory)
      `a buyer or spouse has had the first home owner concession before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, a co-buyer or the spouse or de facto partner of any of you has received the Territory's first home owner concession before
      `a buyer or spouse has owned a home they lived in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, a co-buyer or a spouse or de facto partner of any of you has owned (had a relevant interest in) residential property that one of you lived in
      `a buyer or spouse has had a home grant or concession before, not repaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, a co-buyer or a spouse of any of you has received a first home owner grant, the first home owner discount or concession, the senior, pensioner and carer concession or the principal place of residence rebate, and not repaid it
      `a buyer or spouse has owned residential property anywhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, a co-buyer or a spouse or de facto partner of any of you has ever owned (had a relevant interest in) residential property, in the Territory or elsewhere in Australia
      `a buyer or spouse owned Territory residential property in the last 24 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, a co-buyer or a spouse of any of you owned residential property in the Northern Territory at any time in the 24 months before the contract was signed
      `the Commissioner excuses that Territory property because of a relationship breakdown` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has exempted that Territory property because your marriage or de facto relationship broke down and you no longer have it, or an order, binding agreement or unconditional contract will take it from you (s 89AAB(11))
      `a buyer already has an interest in the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or a co-buyer already has a beneficial interest in the land you are buying
      `the buyers are buying the whole of the property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your co-buyers together are acquiring the whole beneficial interest in the land
      `a buyer is buying as a trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or a co-buyer is buying the land as trustee (for example for a trust or a self-managed super fund)
      `every buyer will live in the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and every co-buyer will live in the home as your principal place of residence for 6 months in a row, starting within the period for occupancy (usually 12 months after you get possession)
      `at least one buyer will live in the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or at least one co-buyer will live in the home as principal place of residence for 6 months in a row, starting within the period for occupancy
      `a buyer who is 60 or older or holds a card will live in the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a buyer who is 60 or older, or who holds an NT concession card, will live in the home as principal place of residence for 6 months in a row, starting within the period for occupancy
      `the Commissioner excuses us from living in the home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner, for special reasons, has exempted you from the requirement to live in the home
      `the home has never been lived in or sold as a home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home has never been occupied or sold as a place of residence (a new home)
      `the home is substantially renovated and not lived in or sold since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home was substantially renovated and sold to you as new residential premises (a taxable supply under the GST Act), and has not been lived in or sold since the renovation
      `the Commissioner has declared the home a qualifying home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has declared the home a qualifying home under s 90AA(2)
      `a buyer has been or will be paid a first home owner grant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or a co-buyer has been paid, is entitled to, or will become entitled to a first home owner grant for this purchase or for building the home (see the First Home Owner Grant Act 2000 encoding)
      `a buyer was paid the grant for a contract made from 1 January 2015 to 6 May 2019` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were paid the first home owner grant for an eligible transaction whose commencement date is on or after 1 January 2015 and before 7 May 2019 (s 89AAC)
      `we get possession within 12 months after settlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you become entitled to possession of the land within 12 months after settlement (or a longer period the Commissioner has approved)
GIVETH A `Home conveyance`
`my home conveyance from my answers` `the date the contract or transfer was first signed` `the price` `the value of the property` `there is already a home on the land` `I am buying off the plan` `every buyer is an individual` `at least one buyer is 18 or older` `at least one buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` `at least one buyer is 60 or older` `at least one buyer holds an NT concession card` `a buyer or spouse has had the first home owner concession before` `a buyer or spouse has owned a home they lived in` `a buyer or spouse has had a home grant or concession before, not repaid` `a buyer or spouse has owned residential property anywhere` `a buyer or spouse owned Territory residential property in the last 24 months` `the Commissioner excuses that Territory property because of a relationship breakdown` `a buyer already has an interest in the land` `the buyers are buying the whole of the property` `a buyer is buying as a trustee` `every buyer will live in the home` `at least one buyer will live in the home` `a buyer who is 60 or older or holds a card will live in the home` `the Commissioner excuses us from living in the home` `the home has never been lived in or sold as a home` `the home is substantially renovated and not lived in or sold since` `the Commissioner has declared the home a qualifying home` `a buyer has been or will be paid a first home owner grant` `a buyer was paid the grant for a contract made from 1 January 2015 to 6 May 2019` `we get possession within 12 months after settlement` MEANS
    `Home conveyance` WITH
        `the date first executed`                                                                                IS `the date the contract or transfer was first signed`
        `the consideration`                                                                                      IS `the price`
        `the unencumbered value`                                                                                 IS `the value of the property`
        `there is a home on the land at the relevant time`                                                       IS `there is already a home on the land`
        `it is an off-the-plan contract`                                                                         IS `I am buying off the plan`
        `every conveyee is an individual`                                                                        IS `every buyer is an individual`
        `at least one conveyee is 18 or older, or is exempted from the age requirement`                          IS `at least one buyer is 18 or older`
        `at least one conveyee is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`                                   IS `at least one buyer is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`
        `at least one conveyee is 60 or older at the relevant time`                                              IS `at least one buyer is 60 or older`
        `at least one conveyee holds an NT pensioner, carer or concession scheme card`                           IS `at least one buyer holds an NT concession card`
        `a conveyee or spouse has received the first home owner concession before`                               IS `a buyer or spouse has had the first home owner concession before`
        `a conveyee or spouse has had a relevant interest in a residence they occupied`                          IS `a buyer or spouse has owned a home they lived in`
        `a conveyee or spouse has received a grant, discount, concession or rebate before, not repaid`           IS `a buyer or spouse has had a home grant or concession before, not repaid`
        `a conveyee or spouse has had a relevant interest in residential property`                               IS `a buyer or spouse has owned residential property anywhere`
        `a conveyee or spouse had a relevant interest in Territory residential property in the 24 months before` IS `a buyer or spouse owned Territory residential property in the last 24 months`
        `the Commissioner exempts that Territory interest for a relationship breakdown`                          IS `the Commissioner excuses that Territory property because of a relationship breakdown`
        `a conveyee already has a beneficial interest in the land`                                               IS `a buyer already has an interest in the land`
        `the conveyees will acquire the whole beneficial interest in the land`                                   IS `the buyers are buying the whole of the property`
        `a conveyee will acquire an interest in the land as trustee`                                             IS `a buyer is buying as a trustee`
        `every conveyee will occupy the home as their principal place of residence`                              IS `every buyer will live in the home`
        `at least one conveyee will occupy the home as their principal place of residence`                       IS `at least one buyer will live in the home`
        `a conveyee who is 60 or older or holds a card will occupy the home`                                     IS `a buyer who is 60 or older or holds a card will live in the home`
        `the Commissioner exempts the conveyees from the occupancy requirement`                                  IS `the Commissioner excuses us from living in the home`
        `the home has not been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence`                              IS `the home has never been lived in or sold as a home`
        `the home is substantially renovated new residential premises not occupied or sold since`                IS `the home is substantially renovated and not lived in or sold since`
        `the Commissioner declares the home a qualifying home`                                                   IS `the Commissioner has declared the home a qualifying home`
        `a conveyee has been paid, is entitled to or will become entitled to a first home owner grant`           IS `a buyer has been or will be paid a first home owner grant`
        `the conveyee is paid the grant for a transaction that commenced from 1 January 2015 to 6 May 2019`      IS `a buyer was paid the grant for a contract made from 1 January 2015 to 6 May 2019`
        `the conveyees become entitled to possession within 12 months after settlement`                          IS `we get possession within 12 months after settlement`

GIVEN `the contract replaces one signed before 1 July 2022, or follows an option from before then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your contract replaces an earlier one for the same or similar land signed before 1 July 2022, or you or the seller had an option over the land granted before 1 July 2022
      `we are buying land owned by a building contractor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the contract, you agree to acquire title to and the whole beneficial interest in land owned by a licensed residential building contractor
      `the builder agrees to convey the land to us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the contract, the building contractor agrees to transfer the land to you
      `the builder agrees to build, finish or hand over a detached new home on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the contract, the building contractor agrees to build or place a detached new home on the land, finish a partly built one, or transfer a completed one that has never been lived in or sold
      `the builder owns the land before signing or will before settlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the building contractor owns the land just before the contract is signed, or will just before settlement
      `the builder bought the lot from its developer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the building contractor bought the land from the person who developed it as a residential lot
      `the builder paid duty when buying the lot` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the building contractor paid stamp duty on the land's dutiable value when buying it from the developer
GIVETH A `New home from a building contractor`
`the builder's side from my answers` `the contract replaces one signed before 1 July 2022, or follows an option from before then` `we are buying land owned by a building contractor` `the builder agrees to convey the land to us` `the builder agrees to build, finish or hand over a detached new home on it` `the builder owns the land before signing or will before settlement` `the builder bought the lot from its developer` `the builder paid duty when buying the lot` MEANS
    `New home from a building contractor` WITH
        `it replaces a conveyance first executed before 1 July 2022, or rests on an option granted before then`            IS `the contract replaces one signed before 1 July 2022, or follows an option from before then`
        `the conveyees agree to acquire title to and the whole beneficial interest in land owned by a building contractor` IS `we are buying land owned by a building contractor`
        `the building contractor agrees to convey the land to the conveyees`                                               IS `the builder agrees to convey the land to us`
        `the building contractor agrees to build, place, complete or convey a detached, new home on the land`              IS `the builder agrees to build, finish or hand over a detached new home on it`
        `the building contractor owns the land before execution, or will before settlement`                                IS `the builder owns the land before signing or will before settlement`
        `the building contractor bought the land from the person who developed it as a residential lot`                    IS `the builder bought the lot from its developer`
        `the building contractor paid duty on the land's dutiable value when buying it from the developer`                 IS `the builder paid duty when buying the lot`

GIVEN `the date the registration certificate is issued` IS A DATE @desc The day the certificate of registration is to be issued, as a date (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-15)
      `I bought it in an arm's length sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are registering the vehicle after buying it in an ordinary sale at arm's length (answer no for a gift, a sale between relatives at a reduced price, or bringing your own vehicle)
      `the price, with deposit, trade-in and added equipment` IS A NUMBER @desc What you paid for the vehicle and any equipment fitted or added before registration, including any deposit and trade-in allowance and GST, in Australian dollars
      `the dealer delivery charges` IS A NUMBER @desc Any dealer delivery charges you paid, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `its market value when the deal was made` IS A NUMBER @desc The vehicle's market value with its equipment on the day the transaction was entered into, in Australian dollars (used only if it was not an arm's length sale)
      `its market value when I apply` IS A NUMBER @desc The vehicle's market value with its equipment on the day you apply for registration, in Australian dollars (used only if it was not an arm's length sale)
      `it is an electric vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle uses an electric motor for propulsion and takes and stores energy from an external source of electricity (battery electric or plug-in hybrid), and has no hydrogen fuel cell
GIVETH A `Vehicle registration`
`my registration from my answers` `the date the registration certificate is issued` `I bought it in an arm's length sale` `the price, with deposit, trade-in and added equipment` `the dealer delivery charges` `its market value when the deal was made` `its market value when I apply` `it is an electric vehicle` MEANS
    `Vehicle registration` WITH
        `the date the certificate is issued`                                               IS `the date the registration certificate is issued`
        `it is a transfer by a sale and purchase at arm's length`                          IS `I bought it in an arm's length sale`
        `the amount for which the vehicle and its additional equipment was sold`           IS `the price, with deposit, trade-in and added equipment`
        `the dealer delivery charges paid`                                                 IS `the dealer delivery charges`
        `the market value with additional equipment when the transaction was entered into` IS `its market value when the deal was made`
        `the market value with additional equipment when the application is made`          IS `its market value when I apply`
        `it is an electric motor vehicle`                                                  IS `it is an electric vehicle`

GIVEN `it was last registered in my name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle was last registered in your name, in the Territory or elsewhere, even if that registration has expired (for example when you move to the Territory)
      `it seats 12 or more and I have never paid duty on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle seats 12 or more people and you have never paid stamp duty on it anywhere in Australia
      `it was a gift from my spouse, parent, child or stepchild` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle came to you wholly as a gift from the person it was last registered to, and you are their spouse, de facto partner, parent, child or stepchild (or it passes to or from such a relative jointly with them)
      `it comes to me from a deceased estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the executor or administrator of a deceased person's estate registering it to transfer to a beneficiary or to sell in winding up the estate, or you are the beneficiary entitled to it
      `it is a motorised wheelchair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is a motorised wheelchair
      `it is a trailer or caravan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is a trailer (a caravan is a trailer)
      `the trailer's gross vehicle mass in tonnes` IS A NUMBER @desc The trailer's gross vehicle mass in tonnes (0 if it is not a trailer)
      `I am a veteran on the special rate or the extreme disablement adjustment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a veteran eligible to receive a pension at the rate in s 22(4) or s 24(4) of the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986 (see the Veterans' Entitlements Act encoding)
      `the vehicle is for my non-commercial use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is for your own non-commercial use
GIVETH A `Vehicle exemption facts`
`my vehicle exemption facts from my answers` `it was last registered in my name` `it seats 12 or more and I have never paid duty on it` `it was a gift from my spouse, parent, child or stepchild` `it comes to me from a deceased estate` `it is a motorised wheelchair` `it is a trailer or caravan` `the trailer's gross vehicle mass in tonnes` `I am a veteran on the special rate or the extreme disablement adjustment` `the vehicle is for my non-commercial use` MEANS
    `Vehicle exemption facts` WITH
        `it is issued to the person in whose name the vehicle was last registered`                                       IS `it was last registered in my name`
        `it seats 12 or more and the applicant has never paid stamp duty on it`                                          IS `it seats 12 or more and I have never paid duty on it`
        `it follows a gift to the spouse, parent, child or stepchild of the last registered owner, or jointly with them` IS `it was a gift from my spouse, parent, child or stepchild`
        `it is issued to the executor, administrator or a beneficiary of a deceased estate, for the estate`              IS `it comes to me from a deceased estate`
        `the vehicle is a motorised wheelchair`                                                                          IS `it is a motorised wheelchair`
        `the vehicle is a trailer or caravan`                                                                            IS `it is a trailer or caravan`
        `the trailer's gross vehicle mass, in tonnes`                                                                    IS `the trailer's gross vehicle mass in tonnes`
        `it is issued to a veteran eligible for a pension at the VEA s 22(4) or 24(4) rate`                              IS `I am a veteran on the special rate or the extreme disablement adjustment`
        `the vehicle is for the veteran's non-commercial use`                                                            IS `the vehicle is for my non-commercial use`

§§ `Buying a home in the Territory -- the duty`

@export What is the dutiable value of my home purchase: the greater of the price and the property's value (Stamp Duty Act 1978 (NT) s 4AB)?
GIVEN `the price` IS A NUMBER @desc The price you are paying for the property, in Australian dollars, including any GST; 0 if it is a gift
      `the value of the property` IS A NUMBER @desc The full market value of the property free of any mortgage or other encumbrance, in Australian dollars, including GST (if you do not know it, give the price)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the dutiable value of my home purchase` IS
    `the dutiable value` `the price` `the value of the property`

@export How much stamp duty is charged on my Northern Territory home purchase before any concession or exemption (Schedule 1 cl 1(2))?
GIVEN `the date the contract or transfer was first signed` IS A DATE @desc The day the first document for your purchase (usually the contract) was signed by everyone, as a date (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-15)
      `the price` IS A NUMBER @desc The price you are paying for the property, in Australian dollars, including any GST; 0 if it is a gift
      `the value of the property` IS A NUMBER @desc The full market value of the property free of any mortgage or other encumbrance, in Australian dollars, including GST (if you do not know it, give the price)
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
DECIDE `How much duty is charged on my home before any concession or exemption` IS
    `the Schedule 1 duty on a conveyance first executed on` `the date the contract or transfer was first signed` (`the dutiable value` `the price` `the value of the property`)

@export Is any Part 5 Division 2 home concession (first home owner concession or discount, Territory home owner discount, senior, pensioner and carer concession, principal place of residence rebate) still open for a purchase signed on this date (s 88A)?
GIVEN `the date the contract or transfer was first signed` IS A DATE @desc The day the first document for your purchase (usually the contract) was signed by everyone, as a date (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-15)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is any Part 5 Division 2 home concession still open for my purchase date` IF
    `Part 5 Division 2 applies to a conveyance first executed on` `the date the contract or transfer was first signed`

@export Which Northern Territory home concession do I get on my purchase, if any, after s 90B allows only the one of greatest benefit (Part 5 Division 2)?
