@export We are joint tenants transferring between ourselves (one owner keeps an interest): how much duty is charged (Schedule 1 cl 1(3), s 4AC)?
GIVEN `the date the contract or transfer was first signed` IS A DATE @desc The day the first document for your purchase (usually the contract) was signed by everyone, as a date (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-15)
      `the value of the whole property` IS A NUMBER @desc The dutiable value of the whole property held or to be held jointly, in Australian dollars
      `the share that passes to the new owner` IS A NUMBER @desc The share of the property not kept by the owners who are transferring, as a fraction (for example 0.5 when two joint owners transfer to one of them, or when a sole owner adds a joint owner)
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
DECIDE `How much duty is charged on a transfer between joint owners` IS
    `the Schedule 1 cl 1(3) duty on a joint tenancy conveyance first executed on` `the date the contract or transfer was first signed` (`the value of a share in property held in common` `the value of the whole property` `the share that passes to the new owner`)

@export Who must pay the duty on my transaction (s 50, s 9(7))?
GIVEN `what is being transferred to me` IS A `Kind of dutiable transaction` @desc One of: a conveyance (a transfer or agreement to transfer property); a lease; a transaction for which the Act makes no particular party liable
GIVETH A `Who is liable`
DECIDE `Who must pay the duty` IS
    `who is liable for the duty on` `what is being transferred to me`

@export Within how many days after the contract or transfer is first signed must I lodge it with the Commissioner for assessment, even if it is exempt (s 9(1), (3))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many days after signing must I lodge my transfer` IS
    `the days to lodge a dutiable instrument`

@export By how many days after the contract or transfer is first signed must I pay the duty (s 9(5), (6))?
GIVEN `the days from signing to a later date fixed in my notice of assessment` IS A NUMBER @desc If your notice of assessment fixes a later date for payment, how many days after first signing that date is (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `By how many days after signing must I pay the duty` IS
    `the days to pay the duty` `the days from signing to a later date fixed in my notice of assessment`

§§ `Living in the home -- occupancy, notice and reassessment`

-- Arises only if you received a home concession or the s 90D exemption, which require you to live in the home.

@export Within how many months after I become entitled to possession must I start living in the home (the period for occupancy, s 88(1))?
GIVEN `the state of the home when I signed` IS A `The home at the relevant time` @desc One of: a home is built on the land; no home yet: the conveyees are owner builders or have a comprehensive home building contract; no home yet: the conveyees have an off-the-plan contract
      `the months from possession to completion of the home` IS A NUMBER @desc If the home is still to be built by you or under a comprehensive home building contract, how many months after you get possession it is completed (0 otherwise)
      `a longer period the Commissioner approved, in months` IS A NUMBER @desc A longer period for occupancy the Commissioner has approved for special reasons, in months after possession (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many months after possession must I start living in the home` IS
    `the period for occupancy, in months after possession` `the state of the home when I signed` `the months from possession to completion of the home` `a longer period the Commissioner approved, in months`

@export For how many months in a row must I live in the home as my principal place of residence (the prescribed period, s 88(1))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `For how many months in a row must I live in the home` IS
    `the prescribed period, in months`

@export I will not, or did not, live in the home as my concession or exemption required: must I tell the Commissioner, and within how many days (ss 89(3), 89AA(6), 89AAB(7), 89A(3), 90(3), 90D(5))?
GIVEN `what I received` IS A `Occupancy provision` @desc What you received: one of s 89(3) -- first home owner concession; s 89AA(6) -- first home owner discount; s 89AAB(7) -- Territory home owner discount; s 89A(3) -- senior, pensioner and carer concession; s 90(3) -- principal place of residence rebate; s 90D(5) -- exemption for a new home from a building contractor
      `I will not or did not live in the home as required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have failed, or it has become apparent that you will fail, to live in the home as your principal place of residence for the required 6 months starting within the period for occupancy
      `none of the buyers will or did live in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every buyer has failed, or will fail, to live in the home as required
      `another buyer has already told the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a co-buyer has already given the Commissioner written notice of the failure
      `I am exempt from the requirement to live in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have an exemption from the requirement to live in the home (for example the Commissioner excused you, or under s 89A(11AA) or s 90(8A) because a co-buyer lives there)
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
DECIDE `Must I tell the Commissioner that I will not live in the home` IS
    IF `the conveyee must give notice of the failure to occupy` `what I received` `my failure from my answers`
    THEN `yes: written notice to the Commissioner within this many days after it first becomes apparent, or a fine of up to this many penalty units` `the days to notify a failure to occupy` `the maximum penalty for not notifying, in penalty units`
    ELSE `no notice is required of me`
    WHERE
        -- The last two fields are not read by the notice rule: fixed placeholders.
        `my failure from my answers` MEANS
            `Occupancy failure` WITH
                `this conveyee fails or will fail to occupy`                         IS `I will not or did not live in the home as required`
                `every conveyee fails or will fail to occupy`                        IS `none of the buyers will or did live in it`
                `another conveyee has already given the notice`                      IS `another buyer has already told the Commissioner`
                `this conveyee has an exemption from the occupancy requirement`      IS `I am exempt from the requirement to live in it`
                `the failure has occurred`                                           IS FALSE
                `the Commissioner is of the opinion there are special reasons not to reassess` IS FALSE

@export I did not live in the home as required: must the Commissioner reassess my duty without the concession or exemption, even after the usual 5-year limit (ss 89(4), 89AAB(4), 89A(6), 90(4), 90D(8))?
GIVEN `what I received` IS A `Occupancy provision` @desc What you received: one of s 89(3) -- first home owner concession; s 89AA(6) -- first home owner discount; s 89AAB(7) -- Territory home owner discount; s 89A(3) -- senior, pensioner and carer concession; s 90(3) -- principal place of residence rebate; s 90D(5) -- exemption for a new home from a building contractor
      `I will not or did not live in the home as required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have failed, or it has become apparent that you will fail, to live in the home as your principal place of residence for the required 6 months starting within the period for occupancy
      `none of the buyers will or did live in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every buyer has failed, or will fail, to live in the home as required
      `another buyer has already told the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a co-buyer has already given the Commissioner written notice of the failure
      `I am exempt from the requirement to live in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have an exemption from the requirement to live in the home (for example the Commissioner excused you, or under s 89A(11AA) or s 90(8A) because a co-buyer lives there)
      `the failure has happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the failure to live in the home has actually happened (not only become likely)
      `the Commissioner sees special reasons not to reassess` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is of the opinion that there are special reasons for not reassessing your duty
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Commissioner reassess my duty because I did not live in the home` IF
    `the Commissioner must reassess after the failure to occupy` `what I received` `my failure from my answers`
    WHERE
        `my failure from my answers` MEANS
            `Occupancy failure` WITH
                `this conveyee fails or will fail to occupy`                         IS `I will not or did not live in the home as required`
                `every conveyee fails or will fail to occupy`                        IS `none of the buyers will or did live in it`
                `another conveyee has already given the notice`                      IS `another buyer has already told the Commissioner`
                `this conveyee has an exemption from the occupancy requirement`      IS `I am exempt from the requirement to live in it`
                `the failure has occurred`                                           IS `the failure has happened`
                `the Commissioner is of the opinion there are special reasons not to reassess` IS `the Commissioner sees special reasons not to reassess`

@export My duty was assessed with a home concession and the first home owner grant was paid to me afterwards: must the Commissioner reassess my duty without the concession (ss 90A(2), 90AB(2))?
GIVEN `the concession my duty was assessed with` IS A `Home concession` @desc The concession your duty was assessed with: the first home owner concession (s 89); the first home owner discount (s 89AA); the Territory home owner discount (s 89AAB); the senior, pensioner and carer concession (s 89A); or the principal place of residence rebate (s 90)
      `the first home owner grant was paid to me afterwards` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner later authorised payment of a first home owner grant to you for this purchase or for building the home
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Commissioner take my concession back because the grant was paid` IF
    `the Commissioner must reassess without the concession once the grant is paid` `the concession my duty was assessed with` `the first home owner grant was paid to me afterwards`

§§ `Transfers that are exempt`

-- Each arises only in its own situation: a separation, an inheritance, a gift to a Special Disability Trust, or adding a spouse to the title.

@export Is the transfer of property to me in a property settlement with my former spouse or de facto partner exempt from duty (s 91: an order or binding financial agreement within 12 months)?
GIVEN `we are or were married or in a de facto relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the other party to the transfer are or were married or in a de facto relationship under the Family Law Act 1975
      `the date of the transfer` IS A DATE @desc The date of the transfer to you, as a date (ISO 8601)
      `the order or agreement` IS A `Settlement instrument` @desc One of: a Family Court order under Part VIII or VIIIAB of the Family Law Act; a binding financial agreement under Part VIIIA or VIIIAB of the Family Law Act; no order or agreement yet
      `the date of the order or agreement` IS A DATE @desc The date the Family Court order or the binding financial agreement was made, as a date (ISO 8601)
      `the transfer came after the relationship broke down for good` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the transfer happened after the marriage or de facto relationship broke down irretrievably
      `the transfer matches the order or agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the terms of the transfer are consistent with the order or agreement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my property settlement with my former partner exempt` IF
    `the conveyance is exempt under s 91` (`Relationship settlement` WITH `the parties are or were married or in a de facto relationship under the Family Law Act` IS `we are or were married or in a de facto relationship`, `the date of the conveyance` IS `the date of the transfer`, `the instrument` IS `the order or agreement`, `the date the order was made or the agreement was made` IS `the date of the order or agreement`, `the conveyance occurred after the relationship irretrievably broke down` IS `the transfer came after the relationship broke down for good`, `the terms of the conveyance are consistent with the order or agreement` IS `the transfer matches the order or agreement`)

@export I paid duty on my property settlement before the order or agreement was made: must the Commissioner refund it (s 91(3))?
GIVEN `we are or were married or in a de facto relationship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the other party to the transfer are or were married or in a de facto relationship under the Family Law Act 1975
      `the date of the transfer` IS A DATE @desc The date of the transfer to you, as a date (ISO 8601)
      `the order or agreement` IS A `Settlement instrument` @desc One of: a Family Court order under Part VIII or VIIIAB of the Family Law Act; a binding financial agreement under Part VIIIA or VIIIAB of the Family Law Act; no order or agreement yet
      `the date of the order or agreement` IS A DATE @desc The date the Family Court order or the binding financial agreement was made, as a date (ISO 8601)
      `the transfer came after the relationship broke down for good` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the transfer happened after the marriage or de facto relationship broke down irretrievably
      `the transfer matches the order or agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the terms of the transfer are consistent with the order or agreement
      `I paid duty on the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you paid duty on the transfer before it became exempt
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Commissioner refund the duty I paid on my settlement` IF
    `the Commissioner must refund the duty under s 91(3)` (`Relationship settlement` WITH `the parties are or were married or in a de facto relationship under the Family Law Act` IS `we are or were married or in a de facto relationship`, `the date of the conveyance` IS `the date of the transfer`, `the instrument` IS `the order or agreement`, `the date the order was made or the agreement was made` IS `the date of the order or agreement`, `the conveyance occurred after the relationship irretrievably broke down` IS `the transfer came after the relationship broke down for good`, `the terms of the conveyance are consistent with the order or agreement` IS `the transfer matches the order or agreement`) `I paid duty on the transfer`

@export Is the transfer of property to me as a beneficiary of a deceased estate exempt from duty (Schedule 2 item 6(d))?
GIVEN `the executor or administrator transfers it to me under the will or the intestacy rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the transfer is made by the executor of the will or administrator of the estate to you as a beneficiary, in accordance with the will or the rules of intestate distribution
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the transfer to me from a deceased estate exempt` IF
    `the conveyance is exempt under Schedule 2 item 6(d)` `the executor or administrator transfers it to me under the will or the intestacy rules`

@export Is my gift of property to a Special Disability Trust exempt from duty (Schedule 2 item 6(e))?
GIVEN `nothing of value is given for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether no valuable consideration is given for the transfer
      `it goes to a Special Disability Trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the property goes to a Special Disability Trust as defined in the Social Security Act 1991 or the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986 (see the Social Security Act encoding)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my gift to a Special Disability Trust exempt` IF
    `the conveyance is exempt under Schedule 2 item 6(e)` `nothing of value is given for it` `it goes to a Special Disability Trust`

@export Is the transfer of our home between me and my spouse or de facto partner, so that we own it in equal shares, exempt from duty (Schedule 2 item 7)?
GIVEN `the only two parties are me and my spouse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there are exactly two parties to the transfer, you and your spouse or de facto partner
      `the property is our principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the property is the home you both live in as your principal place of residence
      `nothing is paid for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether no consideration is given for the transfer
      `we will own it in equal shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether after the transfer you will both own the home in equal shares
      `no one else takes an interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether no other person takes an interest under the transfer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the transfer of our home between me and my spouse exempt` IF
    `the conveyance is exempt under Schedule 2 item 7` (`Transfer between spouses` WITH `there are 2 parties and each is the spouse or de facto partner of the other` IS `the only two parties are me and my spouse`, `the property is the parties' principal place of residence` IS `the property is our principal place of residence`, `no consideration is given` IS `nothing is paid for it`, `both will own the home in equal shares` IS `we will own it in equal shares`, `no other person takes an interest` IS `no one else takes an interest`)

§§ `Registering a motor vehicle`

@export What is the dutiable value of the motor vehicle I am registering in the Northern Territory (s 59(1), (1A))?
GIVEN `the date the registration certificate is issued` IS A DATE @desc The day the certificate of registration is to be issued, as a date (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-15)
      `I bought it in an arm's length sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are registering the vehicle after buying it in an ordinary sale at arm's length (answer no for a gift, a sale between relatives at a reduced price, or bringing your own vehicle)
      `the price, with deposit, trade-in and added equipment` IS A NUMBER @desc What you paid for the vehicle and any equipment fitted or added before registration, including any deposit and trade-in allowance and GST, in Australian dollars
      `the dealer delivery charges` IS A NUMBER @desc Any dealer delivery charges you paid, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `its market value when the deal was made` IS A NUMBER @desc The vehicle's market value with its equipment on the day the transaction was entered into, in Australian dollars (used only if it was not an arm's length sale)
      `its market value when I apply` IS A NUMBER @desc The vehicle's market value with its equipment on the day you apply for registration, in Australian dollars (used only if it was not an arm's length sale)
      `it is an electric vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle uses an electric motor for propulsion and takes and stores energy from an external source of electricity (battery electric or plug-in hybrid), and has no hydrogen fuel cell
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the dutiable value of my vehicle` IS
    `the dutiable value of the vehicle` (`my registration from my answers` `the date the registration certificate is issued` `I bought it in an arm's length sale` `the price, with deposit, trade-in and added equipment` `the dealer delivery charges` `its market value when the deal was made` `its market value when I apply` `it is an electric vehicle`)

@export Is the registration of my motor vehicle exempt from stamp duty, and under which item (Schedule 2 item 23)?
GIVEN `it was last registered in my name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle was last registered in your name, in the Territory or elsewhere, even if that registration has expired (for example when you move to the Territory)
      `it seats 12 or more and I have never paid duty on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle seats 12 or more people and you have never paid stamp duty on it anywhere in Australia
      `it was a gift from my spouse, parent, child or stepchild` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle came to you wholly as a gift from the person it was last registered to, and you are their spouse, de facto partner, parent, child or stepchild (or it passes to or from such a relative jointly with them)
      `it comes to me from a deceased estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the executor or administrator of a deceased person's estate registering it to transfer to a beneficiary or to sell in winding up the estate, or you are the beneficiary entitled to it
      `it is a motorised wheelchair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is a motorised wheelchair
      `it is a trailer or caravan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is a trailer (a caravan is a trailer)
      `the trailer's gross vehicle mass in tonnes` IS A NUMBER @desc The trailer's gross vehicle mass in tonnes (0 if it is not a trailer)
      `I am a veteran on the special rate or the extreme disablement adjustment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a veteran eligible to receive a pension at the rate in s 22(4) or s 24(4) of the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986 (see the Veterans' Entitlements Act encoding)
      `the vehicle is for my non-commercial use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is for your own non-commercial use
GIVETH A `Vehicle exemption`
DECIDE `Is my vehicle registration exempt from duty` IS
    `the item 23 exemption for` (`my vehicle exemption facts from my answers` `it was last registered in my name` `it seats 12 or more and I have never paid duty on it` `it was a gift from my spouse, parent, child or stepchild` `it comes to me from a deceased estate` `it is a motorised wheelchair` `it is a trailer or caravan` `the trailer's gross vehicle mass in tonnes` `I am a veteran on the special rate or the extreme disablement adjustment` `the vehicle is for my non-commercial use`)

@export How much stamp duty must I pay to register my motor vehicle in the Northern Territory ($3 per $100 or part, less any electric vehicle concession or exemption)?
GIVEN `the date the registration certificate is issued` IS A DATE @desc The day the certificate of registration is to be issued, as a date (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-15)
      `I bought it in an arm's length sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are registering the vehicle after buying it in an ordinary sale at arm's length (answer no for a gift, a sale between relatives at a reduced price, or bringing your own vehicle)
      `the price, with deposit, trade-in and added equipment` IS A NUMBER @desc What you paid for the vehicle and any equipment fitted or added before registration, including any deposit and trade-in allowance and GST, in Australian dollars
      `the dealer delivery charges` IS A NUMBER @desc Any dealer delivery charges you paid, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `its market value when the deal was made` IS A NUMBER @desc The vehicle's market value with its equipment on the day the transaction was entered into, in Australian dollars (used only if it was not an arm's length sale)
      `its market value when I apply` IS A NUMBER @desc The vehicle's market value with its equipment on the day you apply for registration, in Australian dollars (used only if it was not an arm's length sale)
      `it is an electric vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle uses an electric motor for propulsion and takes and stores energy from an external source of electricity (battery electric or plug-in hybrid), and has no hydrogen fuel cell
      `it was last registered in my name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle was last registered in your name, in the Territory or elsewhere, even if that registration has expired (for example when you move to the Territory)
      `it seats 12 or more and I have never paid duty on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle seats 12 or more people and you have never paid stamp duty on it anywhere in Australia
      `it was a gift from my spouse, parent, child or stepchild` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle came to you wholly as a gift from the person it was last registered to, and you are their spouse, de facto partner, parent, child or stepchild (or it passes to or from such a relative jointly with them)
      `it comes to me from a deceased estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the executor or administrator of a deceased person's estate registering it to transfer to a beneficiary or to sell in winding up the estate, or you are the beneficiary entitled to it
      `it is a motorised wheelchair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is a motorised wheelchair
      `it is a trailer or caravan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is a trailer (a caravan is a trailer)
      `the trailer's gross vehicle mass in tonnes` IS A NUMBER @desc The trailer's gross vehicle mass in tonnes (0 if it is not a trailer)
      `I am a veteran on the special rate or the extreme disablement adjustment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a veteran eligible to receive a pension at the rate in s 22(4) or s 24(4) of the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986 (see the Veterans' Entitlements Act encoding)
      `the vehicle is for my non-commercial use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is for your own non-commercial use
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
DECIDE `How much duty must I pay to register my vehicle` IS
    `the duty payable on the certificate of registration` (`my registration from my answers` `the date the registration certificate is issued` `I bought it in an arm's length sale` `the price, with deposit, trade-in and added equipment` `the dealer delivery charges` `its market value when the deal was made` `its market value when I apply` `it is an electric vehicle`) (`my vehicle exemption facts from my answers` `it was last registered in my name` `it seats 12 or more and I have never paid duty on it` `it was a gift from my spouse, parent, child or stepchild` `it comes to me from a deceased estate` `it is a motorised wheelchair` `it is a trailer or caravan` `the trailer's gross vehicle mass in tonnes` `I am a veteran on the special rate or the extreme disablement adjustment` `the vehicle is for my non-commercial use`)

@export Must I lodge a declaration of the grounds with my application to claim a vehicle exemption or concession (s 61, s 92A(3))?
GIVEN `what I am claiming` IS A `Vehicle claim` @desc One of: an item 23 exemption; the s 92A electric vehicle concession
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I lodge a declaration to claim my vehicle exemption or concession` IF
    `a declaration of the grounds must be lodged with the application (s 61)` `what I am claiming`

@export What is the most I can be fined, in penalty units, for not paying the vehicle duty before registration, or for not declaring the value or notifying the price (ss 57(1), 59(5))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined over vehicle duty, in penalty units` IS
    `the maximum penalty under ss 57(1) and 59(5), in penalty units`

@export I sold my vehicle: within how many days after the transfer must I notify the amount I received (s 59(3))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many days must I notify the price I received for my vehicle` IS
    `the days for the transferor to notify the consideration`

@export The sale of my vehicle was cancelled: must the Commissioner refund the duty I paid on registering it (s 59A)?
GIVEN `the sale was cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the purchase of the vehicle was cancelled
      `I returned the vehicle to the seller` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you returned the vehicle to the person you bought it from
      `I got back everything I paid except the duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all the money refundable on the cancellation, other than the duty, has been refunded to you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will my vehicle duty be refunded if the sale is cancelled` IF
    `the vehicle duty must be refunded under s 59A` `the sale was cancelled` `I returned the vehicle to the seller` `I got back everything I paid except the duty`

§§ `Challenging a duty assessment or a first home owner grant decision (Taxation Administration Act 2007)`

-- Arises only if you disagree with an assessment of duty or with a decision on a first home owner grant.

@export How much of this decision can I object to (TAA ss 107, 109)?
GIVEN `the decision I disagree with` IS A `Kind of decision` @desc One of: an assessment or reassessment of duty; another decision affecting liability to pay duty; a first home owner grant decision; a decision not to make a reassessment; a negotiated assessment
      `it is a reassessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision is a reassessment of an earlier assessment
      `the amount assessed before` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the earlier assessment, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the amount assessed now` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the decision assesses, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of this decision can I object to` IS
    `the amount open to objection` `the decision I disagree with` `it is a reassessment` `the amount assessed before` `the amount assessed now`

@export Within how many days after the notice of the decision must I lodge my written objection (TAA ss 110, 111)?
GIVEN `the Commissioner extended my time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision maker has extended your time to object under s 111
      `the extended number of days` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, the number of days after the notice that you now have (0 if not extended)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many days must I object` IS
    `the days allowed to object` `the Commissioner extended my time` `the extended number of days`

@export My objection is late: can the time be extended (TAA s 111)?
GIVEN `I applied in writing for more time, giving my reasons in full` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied in writing for an extension, setting out fully and in detail why you did not object within 60 days
      `the Commissioner accepts I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision maker is satisfied you have a reasonable excuse
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my late objection still be accepted` IF
    `the time to object may be extended` `I applied in writing for more time, giving my reasons in full` `the Commissioner accepts I had a reasonable excuse`

@export If my objection is disallowed or allowed only in part, where can I take it: NTCAT or the Supreme Court (TAA s 115; a grant decision goes to NTCAT only)?
GIVEN `the decision I disagree with` IS A `Kind of decision` @desc One of: an assessment or reassessment of duty; another decision affecting liability to pay duty; a first home owner grant decision; a decision not to make a reassessment; a negotiated assessment
      `the decision on my objection` IS A `Objection outcome` @desc One of: the objection is allowed in full; the objection is allowed in part only; the objection is disallowed
GIVETH A `Where the objection can go next`
DECIDE `Where can I take my objection next` IS
    `where the objection can go next` `the decision I disagree with` `the decision on my objection`

@export Within how many days after the notice of the decision on my objection must I apply to NTCAT or appeal to the Supreme Court (TAA ss 116, 117)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many days must I apply for review or appeal` IS
    `the days to apply for review or to appeal`

@export Does objecting, or applying for review or appeal, stop the Commissioner collecting the duty in the meantime (TAA s 128)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my objection stop the duty being collected` IF
    `an objection suspends recovery of the tax`

@export Can the Commissioner still reassess my duty, given the 5-year limit (TAA s 21(4))?
GIVEN `the date of my first assessment` IS A DATE @desc The date of the initial assessment of the duty, as a date (ISO 8601)
      `the date of the reassessment` IS A DATE @desc The date of the reassessment (or today), as a date (ISO 8601)
      `it gives effect to a decision on an objection, review or appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the reassessment gives effect to a decision on an objection, review or appeal about the first assessment
      `I did not fully disclose the facts and was assessed too low` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed to make a full and true disclosure of the facts and, as a result, were assessed too low
      `why the Commissioner is reassessing` IS A `Reason for reassessing` @desc One of: a failure to occupy the home (ss 89(4), 89AAB(4), 89A(6), 90(4), 90D(8)); to give a home concession the conveyees would otherwise receive (ss 89(3A), 89AAB(3), 89A(5), 90(3A)); the first home owner grant, after the senior, pensioner and carer concession or the rebate (s 90A); the first home owner grant, after the Territory home owner discount (s 90AB); a sub-sale after a refund or remission (s 56A(5), (6)); a failure to occupy after the first home owner discount (s 89AA); any other reason
      `I applied in writing for the reassessment within 5 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied in writing for the reassessment within 5 years after the first assessment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commissioner still reassess my duty` IF
    `the Commissioner can make the reassessment` (`Reassessment facts` WITH `the date of the initial assessment` IS `the date of my first assessment`, `the date of the reassessment` IS `the date of the reassessment`, `it gives effect to a decision on an objection, review or appeal` IS `it gives effect to a decision on an objection, review or appeal`, `the taxpayer failed to make a full and true disclosure and was assessed too low` IS `I did not fully disclose the facts and was assessed too low`, `the taxation law authorises a reassessment after 5 years` IS (`the Stamp Duty Act authorises the reassessment after 5 years` `why the Commissioner is reassessing`), `the taxpayer applied in writing for the reassessment within 5 years` IS `I applied in writing for the reassessment within 5 years`)

§§ `Penalty tax and interest on late or short payment (Taxation Administration Act 2007)`

-- Arises only if duty was paid late or short (a tax default).

@export How much penalty tax can I be charged on duty I paid late or short (TAA ss 39, 41, 42: 25%, 10%, 75% or 95%, nil under $20)?
GIVEN `the unpaid duty` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of duty you failed to pay on time (the tax default), in dollars
      `it was beyond my control and I fixed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied the default arose from circumstances beyond your control (not just lack of money) and that you took all reasonable steps to fix it once you found it
      `I took reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied you took reasonable care to comply
      `I intentionally disregarded the law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied the default arose wholly or partly from intentional disregard of a taxation law by you or someone acting for you
      `information was concealed or the assessment hindered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied you, or someone acting for you, deliberately concealed or suppressed information or hindered the assessment or investigation
      `I cooperated fully with an investigation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner investigated the default and you cooperated fully
      `I disclosed it fully before any investigation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before any investigation began, your full and immediate disclosure of the default avoided the need for one
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much penalty tax can I be charged` IS
    `the penalty tax` (`Penalty tax facts` WITH `the amount of the tax default` IS `the unpaid duty`, `the default arose from circumstances beyond the taxpayer's control and was rectified` IS `it was beyond my control and I fixed it`, `the taxpayer took reasonable care to comply` IS `I took reasonable care`, `the default arose from intentional disregard of a taxation law` IS `I intentionally disregarded the law`, `information was deliberately concealed or the assessment was hindered` IS `information was concealed or the assessment hindered`, `the Commissioner investigated and the taxpayer cooperated fully` IS `I cooperated fully with an investigation`, `before any investigation, full and immediate disclosure avoided the need for one` IS `I disclosed it fully before any investigation`)

@export What is the least penalty tax I can be left with if the Commissioner reduces it for my cooperation or disclosure (TAA s 41(3)); the Commissioner may also remit more (s 44)?
GIVEN `the unpaid duty` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of duty you failed to pay on time (the tax default), in dollars
      `it was beyond my control and I fixed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied the default arose from circumstances beyond your control (not just lack of money) and that you took all reasonable steps to fix it once you found it
      `I took reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied you took reasonable care to comply
      `I intentionally disregarded the law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied the default arose wholly or partly from intentional disregard of a taxation law by you or someone acting for you
      `information was concealed or the assessment hindered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied you, or someone acting for you, deliberately concealed or suppressed information or hindered the assessment or investigation
      `I cooperated fully with an investigation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner investigated the default and you cooperated fully
      `I disclosed it fully before any investigation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before any investigation began, your full and immediate disclosure of the default avoided the need for one
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the least penalty tax after a reduction for cooperation or disclosure` IS
    `the least penalty tax after a s 41(3) reduction` (`Penalty tax facts` WITH `the amount of the tax default` IS `the unpaid duty`, `the default arose from circumstances beyond the taxpayer's control and was rectified` IS `it was beyond my control and I fixed it`, `the taxpayer took reasonable care to comply` IS `I took reasonable care`, `the default arose from intentional disregard of a taxation law` IS `I intentionally disregarded the law`, `information was deliberately concealed or the assessment was hindered` IS `information was concealed or the assessment hindered`, `the Commissioner investigated and the taxpayer cooperated fully` IS `I cooperated fully with an investigation`, `before any investigation, full and immediate disclosure avoided the need for one` IS `I disclosed it fully before any investigation`)

@export Within how many days must I pay penalty tax (TAA s 43: the period in the notice, at least 14 days)?
GIVEN `the days stated in my notice` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days to pay stated in the notice of assessment imposing the penalty tax
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many days must I pay penalty tax` IS
    `the days to pay penalty tax` `the days stated in my notice`

@export How much interest is charged on my unpaid duty and penalty tax (TAA ss 34-36: market rate plus 8%, daily, nil under $20)?
GIVEN `the unpaid duty` IS A NUMBER @desc The duty unpaid, in dollars
      `the unpaid penalty tax` IS A NUMBER @desc The penalty tax unpaid, in dollars
      `the market interest rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The market interest rate for the financial year, in percent a year (prescribed by regulation, or else the Reserve Bank's average 90-day bank-accepted bill yield for May of the previous financial year; not in the deposited texts)
      `the date the duty fell due` IS A DATE @desc The date of the tax default (when the duty fell due and was not paid), as a date (ISO 8601)
      `the date I pay` IS A DATE @desc The date you pay, as a date (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much interest is charged on my unpaid duty` IS
    `the interest on the tax default` `the unpaid duty` `the unpaid penalty tax` `the market interest rate` `the date the duty fell due` `the date I pay`

